# sys.allow - the census allowlist for this target's system-call schedule (build.sh, DSL_SYSFAIL=1).
#
# After the archive copy is renamed (src/aef_alloc.redefs + src/aef_sys.redefs), every name the copy still
# leaves undefined must be defined in the program set, be an aef_* trampoline, be a sanitizer entry point
# (__asan_ / __ubsan_ / __sanitizer_), or be listed here. These are the pure C library functions zlib 1.4's
# objects reference at the pinned commit (llvm-nm -u over lib/libaef.a in all four flavours, 2026-11-15): none
# makes a system call, so none can touch a file outside the schedule. malloc is not here because the
# allocation map renames it (aef_malloc); free allocates nothing and is not scheduled (src/aef_alloc.redefs).
# strerror formats zlib's error messages from errno; musl's makes no system call. A new name here must be
# argued the same way: one that can reach the kernel belongs in a rename map, not in this list.
__assert_fail
__errno_location
free
memchr
memcpy
memmove
memset
snprintf
strerror
strlen
vsnprintf
